## Target state

After a successful baseline:

- dependency downloads are exceptional;
- source compilation of CI utilities is exceptional;
- unchanged expensive intermediates are reused;
- the same source is not redundantly compiled;
- irrelevant workflows do not run;
- superseded commits stop consuming compute;
- the critical path mostly contains new information;
- expensive exhaustive work runs only where it adds standing;
- successful baseline builds seed useful future reuse;
- cache misses remain correct.

The steady-state goal is to compute the semantic delta introduced by the commit.

## Final execution order

```text
Find -> Fence -> Measure -> Eliminate -> Reuse -> Cache -> Precompile
     -> Parallelize -> Right-size -> Verify -> Measure again -> Receipt -> Replay
```

The objective is not attractive workflow YAML. The objective is the minimum computation necessary to establish all required claims, arranged to establish them in the minimum possible wall-clock time.
